 ## Background
-Uniform Ray Sampling is the default raymarching strategy in the original NeRF paper [S10][S15, unofficial]. It is based on the assumption that without prior knowledge of the scene's density distribution, every point along the ray is equally likely to contribute to the image [S2]. This method is widely used in neural radiance field (NeRF) implementations as the coarse sampling stage [S10].
+Uniform Ray Sampling is the default raymarching strategy in the original NeRF paper [S11][S15, unofficial]. It is based on the assumption that without prior knowledge of the scene's density distribution, every point along the ray is equally likely to contribute to the image [S3]. This method is widely used in neural radiance field (NeRF) implementations as the coarse sampling stage [S3].
 
